-- NOT the L4 prelude: a module of the author's own that happens to be called
-- `prelude.l4`, beside the file that imports it. With JL4_LIBRARY_PATH unset,
-- it outranks the copy compiled into `l4`, so `uses-shadow.l4` imports THIS.
-- Each function has the prelude's name and type and a different body. Before
-- the export asked which module is the library, it lowered these calls as the
-- prelude's (`count(xs)`, `sum(...)`, `every`, `list contains`, `x != null`)
-- while `l4 run` evaluated the bodies below. `shadow marker` is not in the
-- real prelude, so `uses-shadow.l4` type-checks only if this copy won.
GIVEN a    IS A TYPE
      list IS A LIST OF a
GIVETH A NUMBER
count list MEANS 42

GIVEN list IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
sum list MEANS 7

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
      y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
max x y MEANS x PLUS y

GIVEN a    IS A TYPE
      x    IS AN a
      list IS A LIST OF a
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
elem x list MEANS FALSE

GIVEN a    IS A TYPE
      f    IS A FUNCTION FROM a TO BOOLEAN
      list IS A LIST OF a
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
all f list MEANS FALSE

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
      x IS A MAYBE a
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
isJust x MEANS FALSE

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
      x IS A MAYBE a
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
isNothing x MEANS FALSE

GIVETH A NUMBER
`shadow marker` MEANS 1
